{
  "slug": "wmux-orchestrator",
  "name": "Wmux Orchestrator",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Multi-agent task orchestration for Claude Code. Decomposes\ncomplex development tasks into parallel Claude Code agents\ncoordinated through dependency-aware waves with visual terminal\npanes and automated review. Works standalone with native\nsubagents or with wmux for visible agent panes. Features include\ndependency-aware wave planning, file zone enforcement per worker\nto prevent conflicts, and post-orchestration automated review\nwith auto-fix.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **1 agent**, **1 command** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `orchestrate` (Core orchestration skill), `reviewer` (Automated reviewer for wmux orchestrations), `wmux-detect` (Detect if wmux terminal multiplexer is running)\n- **Agents** (1): `wmux-worker` (Worker agent for wmux orchestrated tasks)\n- **Commands** (1): `orchestrate` (Decompose a complex dev task into parallel subtasks and orchestrate multiple Claude Code agents across wmux terminal panes)\n- **Hooks** (4): `PostToolUse`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install wmux-orchestrator@claude-community` from `amirlehmam/wmux-orchestrator`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 1
  },
